1. Permission to Use

Anyone may freely access, download, compile, run, and use LoadEngine for personal, educational, research, and commercial purposes, subject to the conditions of this license.

You are permitted to:
- Use LoadEngine to create games, applications, and interactive projects.
- Sell, publish, distribute, and commercially monetize games and projects created using LoadEngine.
- Use LoadEngine in commercial or non-commercial development workflows.
- Modify your local copy of LoadEngine for personal or internal project use.
- Create custom tools, plugins, extensions, and components that work with LoadEngine.
- Use the engine without paying royalties or obtaining individual permission.

No royalties or fees are required for creating or selling games and other products made with LoadEngine.

2. Source Code Access and Modification

The source code is publicly available through the official repository:
https://github.com/danielSeSa/LoadEngine

Anyone may inspect, study, and modify the source code for permitted purposes. You may maintain private modifications and use them in your own internal projects.

However, access to the source code does not grant permission to independently publish, redistribute, sublicense, or sell the LoadEngine source code or modified versions of the engine.

3. Contributions and Bug Fixes

Community contributions are welcome. Anyone may:
- Report bugs and technical issues.
- Submit bug fixes and performance optimizations.
- Suggest improvements and new features.
- Fork the official GitHub repository strictly for the purpose of developing and submitting Pull Requests to the official repository.

All contributions are subject to review and approval by the project owner. The project owner reserves the right to accept, reject, modify, or decline any contribution at their sole discretion.

Contributor Rights and Grant of License:
Contributors retain copyright ownership of their original contributions. However, by submitting a contribution (including Pull Requests, patches, or code snippets) to the official LoadEngine repository, contributors grant Seyed Daniel Seyed Saadat a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, irrevocable, royalty-free, transferable, and sublicensable license to:
- Use, reproduce, modify, and adapt the contribution.
- Incorporate the contribution into LoadEngine.
- Distribute and commercially license the contribution as part of LoadEngine.
- Maintain, improve, and develop the contribution in future versions.

Contributors warrant that they have the legal right to submit everything they contribute and that their contributions do not infringe upon any third-party rights.

4. Redistribution and Forking Restrictions

Without prior written permission from the copyright owner, you may not:
- Independently redistribute, host, or publish the LoadEngine source code outside of a standard GitHub fork intended for contributing back to the official repository.
- Rebrand, repackage, or publish modified versions or forks of LoadEngine as an independent game engine, software suite, or competing product.
- Distribute standalone copies of the engine editor/binaries or modified versions thereof.
- Sell, sublicense, rent, or commercially distribute LoadEngine itself.
- Remove, obscure, or misrepresent the original copyright and licensing notices.

These restrictions do not prohibit distributing compiled games and applications created with LoadEngine under Section 5.

5. Games and Projects Created with LoadEngine (Mandatory Attribution)

You are free to create, publish, distribute, and commercially sell games and other applications developed using LoadEngine.

You may:
- Sell games made with LoadEngine on any platform (such as Steam, itch.io, Epic Games Store, mobile stores, or independent platforms).
- Keep your game's source code and assets private.
- Use your own branding, trademarks, and intellectual property for your games.
- Distribute compiled runtime components of LoadEngine strictly as bundled within and necessary to operate your game or application.

Mandatory Attribution Requirement:
Any game or interactive application created with LoadEngine and distributed publicly or commercially MUST clearly display the "Made with LoadEngine" notice or the official LoadEngine logo/splash screen at the startup sequence (splash screen) of the application, unless a prior written exemption is obtained from the copyright owner.

You do not need to pay royalties to the LoadEngine copyright owner for games or applications created using the engine.

